(module easyeda2kicad:CAP-ADJ-TH_3P-BD7.6_BFC280811339 (layer F.Cu) (tedit 5DC5F6A4)
	(descr "Vishay BCcomponents BFC280811339, Dia 7.5-7.6mm PP-film THT trimmer, 3-33pF, 250VDC (500VDC/1min test), vertical, round head, TOP AND BOTTOM adjustment (this design uses TOP only). Pad 1 = STATOR (single pad, the fixed plate) - RECOMMENDED for the RF/signal net. Pad 2 = ROTOR (x2 physical pads, same net, the tool-adjusted plate) - RECOMMENDED for GND: tying the tool-exposed rotor to ground keeps hand/blade capacitance off the RF signal while tuning (standard RF practice, not a datasheet requirement). Net assignment is left to schematic capture; this is guidance only. TOP ADJUST: Ø2.5mm slotted round head (screwdriver slot ~0.6mm wide x 0.7mm per Vishay dwg p.2); use a small flat-blade trimming tool, blade width <=0.6mm, non-metallic (plastic/ceramic) preferred to avoid detuning during adjustment - tool material is engineering judgement, not datasheet-stated. Body Ø7.6mm (F.Fab circle), overall height 10mm max board-to-head-top (Vishay dwg p.2). Hole pattern (Vishay dwg p.2, R=Rotor/S=Stator): right-angle L, S at the corner vertex, 5.08mm to each R; matches this footprint's pads exactly. Pulled via easyeda2kicad (LCSC C3273212); pads renumbered and 5 irreducible sub-0.25mm silk artifacts removed by librarian P3 (worst measured gap 0.014mm, could not be narrowed to the 0.15mm JLC floor and clear copper - see LEARNINGS 2026-07-28 fix recipe) - see FILES note in P3 summary.")
	(tags "trimmer variable capacitor RF top-adjust BFC2808")
	(attr through_hole)
	(fp_text reference REF** (at 0 -4.625) (layer F.SilkS)
		(effects (font (size 1 1) (thickness 0.15)))
	)
	(fp_text value CAP-ADJ-TH_3P-BD7.6_BFC280811339 (at 0.000 6.540) (layer F.Fab)
		(effects (font (size 1 1) (thickness 0.15)))
	)
	(fp_text user %R (at 0 0) (layer F.Fab)
		(effects (font (size 1 1) (thickness 0.15)))
	)
	(property "LCSC Part" "C3273212")
